eER_Attribute 3
aName      MultipleChildLimit
aZKey      11041864
aDesc      389
On database access, this is the maximum number of children that will be returned under a parent.  

As an example, consider parent A and child B with MultipleChildLimit of 200. If a particular instance of A is activated that has 300 instances of B under it, only the first 200 instances will be retrieved and the return code of the Activate will notify the application of the condition.␀
